<meta type=article title="Asset HTML Projection" />

<data>
<fig #fig:ext src="images/diagram.png" />
<fig #fig:jpg jpg>JPGdata1</fig>
<fig #fig:svg svg>SVGdata1</fig>
<fig #fig:gif gif>GIFdata1</fig>
<fig #fig:webp webp>WEBPdata1</fig>
<fig #fig:bad bmp>BMPdata1=</fig>
<fig #fig:logo png>iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAQAAAC1HAwCAAAAC0lEQVR42mNk+M9QDwADhgGAWjR9awAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==</fig>
</data>

<section | External assets>

An external asset renders its declared path verbatim: <fig src="@fig:ext" | An external diagram.>

<section | Embedded media types>

JPEG: <fig src="@fig:jpg" | A jpeg.>
SVG: <fig src="@fig:svg" | An svg.>
GIF: <fig src="@fig:gif" | A gif.>
WebP: <fig src="@fig:webp" | A webp.>
Unsupported: <fig src="@fig:bad" | bmp is not a supported embedded format.>

<section | Duplicate placement>

Re-placing one asset is legitimate — see <ref @fig:logo>, shown twice:

<fig src="@fig:logo" | The logo, first placement — the cross-reference anchor.>

<fig src="@fig:logo" | The logo, placed again.>
